# This file is used to manage Python dependencies via pip.
#
# The current design choice is to only pin when necessary. Otherwise, allow updating to the latest version.
# The tradeoff here is we risk breaking changes if/when a dependency version updates, but the benefit is we stay at the
# forefront of new features and bug fixes.
#
# Add new direct (not transitive!) dependencies below (pin versions as needed).
#
# Run `dazel run //:requirements.update` to update requirements.txt without upgrading versions that meet requirements.
#
# Run `dazel run //:requirements.update -- --upgrade` to upgrade to the latest allowed versions.
#
# Run `dazel test //:requirements.test` to test the requirements.txt file is up-to-date.
